#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128994 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129175 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c0559f0c-a1ca-5ba8-a02e-71d584273958" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Double Integral Using Lower and Upper Riemann Sums"}] :question/id #uuid "7caffa88-776d-52e1-8b81-2ebf98aedebc" :question/math-academy-id "e-6122" :question/problem "Let $R = [-1,4]\\times [1,2]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}},\\,{P}_{2}={{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the double integral\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle\\iint\\limits_R f(x,y) \\, \\textrm{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ is a function such that $m_{ij} = M_{ij} = 3$ for all partitions $P$ of $R,$ and $m_{ij}$ and $M_{ij}$ are the minimum and maximum values of $f$ respectively in each subregion $R_{ij}.$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x,y),$ the double integral of $f$ over a rectangular region $R$ is the unique number $I$ (if it exists) such that\n\n$$\nL(f,P) \\leq I \\leq U(f,P)\n$$\n\nover all partitions $P$ of $R,$ where the lower and upper sums respectively are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{m}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} \\\\ U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{M}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand $m_{ij}$ and $M_{ij}$ are the minimum and maximum values of $f$ in each subregion $R_{ij}.$ \n\nNow, since $m_{ij}=M_{ij}=3,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P)=U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}3\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} \\\\  & =3({\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i})({\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}) \\\\  & =3(4-(-1))(2-1) \\\\  & =3\\cdot 5\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =15.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P)=15 & \\le {∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A\\le 15=U(f,P),\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich implies that\n\n$$\n\\iint\\limits_R f(x,y)\\,\\textrm d A = 15.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129039 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129220 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0b9d2e98-8007-51ec-bfb6-cb9b48029a2a" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Double Integral Using the Mean Value of X and Y"}] :question/id #uuid "3464909c-5b04-5cb1-96c9-a409fa105bb9" :question/math-academy-id "e-9494" :question/problem "Let $R = [0,2]\\times [1,3]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)$ be a function defined over $R.$\nThe lower and upper Riemann sums corresponding to an arbitrary partition $P$ of $R$ are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({x}_{i-1}+2{y}_{j-1})\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j},\\, \\\\ U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({x}_{i}+2{y}_{j})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the definition of the double integral in terms of $L(f,P)$ and $U(f,P),$ compute $\\displaystyle\\iint\\limits_R f(x,y)\\,\\textrm d A.$\n\n*Hint: You may wish to make use of the following result:*\n\n$$\n\\sum_{i=1}^m\\sum_{j=1}^n\\left(x_{i-1} + x_i\\right)\\Delta x_i \\Delta y_j = (x_m^2 - x_0^2)(y_n-y_0)\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x,y),$ the double integral of $f$ over a rectangular region $R$ is the unique number $I$ (if it exists) such that\n\n$$\nL(f,P) \\leq I \\leq U(f,P)\n$$\n\nover all partitions $P$ of $R.$\n\nFirst, notice that $\\bar{x}_i = \\dfrac 1 2 (x_{i-1}+x_i)$ will always lie between $x_{i-1}$ and $x_i,$ and similarly $\\bar{y}_j = \\dfrac 1 2 (y_{j-1}+y_j)$ will always lie between $y_{j-1}$ and $y_j.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\nx_{i-1} + {\\color{blue}2}y_{j-1} \\leq \\dfrac{1}{2}(x_{i-1} + x_i) + {\\color{blue}2}\\cdot \\dfrac 1 2 (y_{j-1} + y_j) \\leq x_{i} + {\\color{blue}2}y_{j},\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies to \n\n$$\nx_{i-1} + 2y_{j-1} \\leq \\dfrac{1}{2}(x_{i-1} + x_i) + (y_{j-1} + y_j)\\leq x_{i} + 2y_{j}.\n$$\n\nMultiplying this by $\\Delta x_i\\Delta y_j$ and applying the double summation gives\n\n$$\nL(f,P) \\leq \\sum_{i=1}^m\\sum_{j=1}^n\\left[\\dfrac{1}{2}(x_{i-1} + x_i) + (y_{j-1} + y_j)\\right]\\Delta x_i \\Delta y_j\\leq U(f,P).\n$$\n\nSeparating the sums using the addition and constant multiple rules, we get\n\n$$\nL(f,P) \\leq \\dfrac{1}{2}\\sum_{i=1}^m\\sum_{j=1}^n\\left(x_{i-1} + x_i\\right)\\Delta x_i \\Delta y_j + \\sum_{i=1}^m\\sum_{j=1}^n\\left(y_{j-1} + y_j\\right)\\Delta x_i \\Delta y_j\\leq U(f,P).\n$$\n\nUsing the hint, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} & =\\frac{1}{2}({2}^{2}-{0}^{2})(3-1)=4 \\\\ {\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} & =({3}^{2}-{1}^{2})(2-0)=16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, then:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P)\\le 4+16\\le U(f,P)\\,⟹\\,L(f,P)\\le 20\\le U(f,P)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that \n\n$$\n\\iint\\limits_R f(x,y)\\,\\textrm d A = 20.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129040 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129221 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "89023510-57f4-52f9-90ed-eae07f48f707" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Definition of the Double Integral in Terms of Lower and Upper Riemann Sums"}] :question/id #uuid "e75f2d8e-c165-5a24-942b-7326d7f11f0f" :question/math-academy-id "e-9497" :question/problem "Let $R = [0,1]\\times [1,2]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y) = 12-x-y.$ Further, let \n\n$$\n\\displaystyle I = \\iint\\limits_{R} f(x,y)\\,\\textrm dA\n$$\n\nbe the unique number such that over all rectangular partitions $P$ of $R,$ we have \n$L(f,P)\\:\\leq I \\:\\leq U(f,P),$\nwhere $L(f,P)$ and $U(f,P)$ are the corresponding lower and upper Riemann sums. Write down the upper Riemann sum $U(f,P).$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x,y),$ the double integral of $f$ over a rectangular region $R$ is the unique number $I$ (if it exists) such that\n\n$$\nL(f,P) \\leq I \\leq U(f,P)\n$$\n\nover all partitions $P$ of $R,$ where the lower and upper sums respectively are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{m}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} \\\\ U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{M}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand $m_{ij}$ and $M_{ij}$ are the minimum and maximum values of $f$ respectively in each subregion $R_{ij}.$ \n\nWe need to compute $U(f,P).$ \n\nNotice that for all subregions $R_{ij},$ we have that\n\n- $f(x,y) = 12-x-y$ decreases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y) = 12-x-y$ decreases as $y$ increases.\n\nAs a result, the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *smallest* possible $x$ and the *smallest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *bottom left corner* of each subregion. Therefore,\n\n$$\nM_{ij} = f(x_{i-1}, y_{j-1}) = 12-x_{i-1}-y_{j-1}\n$$\n\nand the upper Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\nU(f,P) = \\sum_{i=1}^m\\sum_{j=1}^n (12-x_{i-1}-y_{j-1})\\Delta x_i \\Delta y_j.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259547 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129221 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "89023510-57f4-52f9-90ed-eae07f48f707" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Definition of the Double Integral in Terms of Lower and Upper Riemann Sums"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1364be74-3e75-52af-960e-229bb98bd9e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{x}_{i}^{2}+{y}_{j}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256956} {:answer/id #uuid "4e8ec975-eb9e-5775-a225-7b96aa8b7e5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{x}_{i-1}^{2}+{y}_{j-1}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257455} {:answer/id #uuid "97668454-4c69-5ab4-ae38-17be9a3c62f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{x}_{i}^{2}+{y}_{j-1}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258119} {:answer/id #uuid "bd2599df-a436-570d-bd42-8f1ba1996faf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of the options is correct" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258433} {:answer/id #uuid "d5471584-54b5-502a-b8f4-8e0f65d7c1ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{x}_{i-1}^{2}+{y}_{j}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258648}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1364be74-3e75-52af-960e-229bb98bd9e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{x}_{i}^{2}+{y}_{j}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256956} :answer-field/id #uuid "1f4a0338-aa97-5cbb-bcbf-a27f90ade86a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259085}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4c92a16d-8ec0-5bb7-a1d3-67db8dee714c" :question/math-academy-id "q-123737" :question/problem "Let $R=[1,3]\\times [2,4]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=3{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}.$ Further, let \n\n$$\nI={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nbe the unique number such that over all rectangular partitions $P$ of $R,$ we have \n$L(f,P)\\,\\le I\\,\\le U(f,P),$\nwhere $L(f,P)$ and $U(f,P)$ are the corresponding lower and upper Riemann sums, and \n\n$$\nU(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\boxed{}\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\,.\n$$\n\nWhat expression is missing from the double summation above?" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x,y),$ the double integral of $f$ over a rectangular region $R$ is the unique number $I$ (if it exists) such that\n\n$$\nL(f,P)\\le I\\le U(f,P),\n$$\n\nover all partitions $P$ of $R,$ where the lower and upper sums respectively are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{m}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} \\\\ U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{M}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand ${m}_{ij}$ and ${M}_{ij}$ are the minimum and maximum values of $f$ respectively in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nWe need to compute $U(f,P).$ \n\nNotice that for all subregions ${R}_{ij},$ we have that\n\n- $f(x,y)=3{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}$ increases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=3{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}$ increases as $y$ increases.\n\nAs a result, the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *largest* possible $x$ and the *largest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *top right corner* of each subregion. Therefore,\n\n$$\n{M}_{ij}=f({x}_{i},{y}_{j})=3{x}_{i}^{2}+{y}_{j}^{2}\n$$\n\nand the upper Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\nU(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(3{x}_{i}^{2}+{y}_{j}^{2})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\n$$\n\nSo, the missing expression is $3{x}_{i}^{2}+{y}_{j}^{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259549 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129221 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "89023510-57f4-52f9-90ed-eae07f48f707" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Definition of the Double Integral in Terms of Lower and Upper Riemann Sums"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09f2e2ce-1f99-5cc7-b2d1-9ac1d670b688" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10+{y}_{j}-3{x}_{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256872} {:answer/id #uuid "3f66d925-6561-5588-8fd7-4530cc7c41b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10+{y}_{j}-3{x}_{i-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257352} {:answer/id #uuid "a5972f0d-e79f-515c-a458-75f95f6077f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of the options is correct" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258225} {:answer/id #uuid "bf6de38b-3230-5053-a855-563b75b0c20b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10+{y}_{j-1}-3{x}_{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258452} {:answer/id #uuid "f24dc428-1a7f-54f1-a935-f54e25d6c6f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10+{y}_{j-1}-3{x}_{i-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258891}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3f66d925-6561-5588-8fd7-4530cc7c41b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10+{y}_{j}-3{x}_{i-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257352} :answer-field/id #uuid "799f8cc2-5f9e-5760-8c56-6a81978126ce" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259238}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8df0d876-87f5-5ec6-b4ea-583e00a0fa95" :question/math-academy-id "q-123741" :question/problem "Let $R=[1,3]\\times [-2,-1]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=10+y-3x.$ Further, let \n\n$$\nI={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nbe the unique number such that over all rectangular partitions $P$ of $R,$ we have \n$L(f,P)\\,\\le I\\,\\le U(f,P),$\nwhere $L(f,P)$ and $U(f,P)$ are the corresponding lower and upper Riemann sums, and \n\n$$\nU(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\boxed{}\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\,.\n$$\n\nWhat expression is missing from the double summation above?" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x,y),$ the double integral of $f$ over a rectangular region $R$ is the unique number $I$ (if it exists) such that\n\n$$\nL(f,P)\\le I\\le U(f,P),\n$$\n\nover all partitions $P$ of $R,$ where the lower and upper sums respectively are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{m}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} \\\\ U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{M}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand ${m}_{ij}$ and ${M}_{ij}$ are the minimum and maximum values of $f$ respectively in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nWe need to compute $U(f,P).$ \n\nNotice that for all subregions ${R}_{ij},$ we have that\n\n- $f(x,y)=10+y-3x$ decreases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=10+y-3x$ increases as $y$ increases.\n\nAs a result, the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *smallest* possible $x$ and the *largest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *top left corner* of each subregion. Therefore,\n\n$$\n{M}_{ij}=f({x}_{i-1},{y}_{j})=10+{y}_{j}-3{x}_{i-1}\n$$\n\nand the upper Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\nU(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(10+{y}_{j}-3{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\n$$\n\nSo, the missing expression is $10+{y}_{j}-3{x}_{i-1}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259550 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129221 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "89023510-57f4-52f9-90ed-eae07f48f707" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Definition of the Double Integral in Terms of Lower and Upper Riemann Sums"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d4967b5-cf10-5833-be5f-85f6c07ea0e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}_{i}^{2}+2{y}_{j}^{2}+{y}_{j}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256911} {:answer/id #uuid "3fa5c5d6-df83-5c27-a35f-92f8050433d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of the options is correct" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257353} {:answer/id #uuid "8281285e-8b82-566b-87ce-26718f43f9ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}_{i-1}^{2}+2{y}_{j}^{2}+{y}_{j}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257939} {:answer/id #uuid "bf0d4f2c-d13e-5dbc-86bd-da31ba6c7bda" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}_{i}^{2}+2{y}_{j-1}^{2}+{y}_{j-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258447} {:answer/id #uuid "e856153e-d8c9-5ff1-bd72-326b4aa7c033" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}_{i-1}^{2}+2{y}_{j-1}^{2}+{y}_{j-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258796}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e856153e-d8c9-5ff1-bd72-326b4aa7c033" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}_{i-1}^{2}+2{y}_{j-1}^{2}+{y}_{j-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258796} :answer-field/id #uuid "fefce3eb-55ec-5c40-a1e4-1147a9146a22" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259482}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2de9d676-815f-5c88-935f-91c621a59e79" :question/math-academy-id "q-123742" :question/problem "Let $R=[1,2]\\times [2,6]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)={x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}+y.$ Further, let \n\n$$\nI={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nbe the unique number such that over all rectangular partitions $P$ of $R,$ we have \n$L(f,P)\\,\\le I\\,\\le U(f,P),$\nwhere $L(f,P)$ and $U(f,P)$ are the corresponding lower and upper Riemann sums, and \n\n$$\nL(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\boxed{}\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\,.\n$$\n\nWhat expression is missing from the double summation above?" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x,y),$ the double integral of $f$ over a rectangular region $R$ is the unique number $I$ (if it exists) such that\n\n$$\nL(f,P)\\le I\\le U(f,P),\n$$\n\nover all partitions $P$ of $R,$ where the lower and upper sums respectively are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{m}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} \\\\ U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{M}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand ${m}_{ij}$ and ${M}_{ij}$ are the minimum and maximum values of $f$ respectively in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nWe need to compute $L(f,P).$ \n\nNotice that for all subregions ${R}_{ij},$ we have that\n\n- $f(x,y)={x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}+y$ increases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)={x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}+y$ increases as $y$ increases.\n\nAs a result, the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *smallest* possible $x$ and the *smallest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *bottom left corner* of each subregion. Therefore,\n\n$$\n{m}_{ij}=f({x}_{i-1},{y}_{j-1})={x}_{i-1}^{2}+2{y}_{j-1}^{2}+{y}_{j-1}\n$$\n\nand the lower Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\nL(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({x}_{i-1}^{2}+2{y}_{j-1}^{2}+{y}_{j-1})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\n$$\n\nSo, the missing expression is ${x}_{i-1}^{2}+2{y}_{j-1}^{2}+{y}_{j-1}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129423 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129221 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "89023510-57f4-52f9-90ed-eae07f48f707" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Definition of the Double Integral in Terms of Lower and Upper Riemann Sums"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b20d747a-3bde-527b-a1e2-f12b7fb6e6c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x_{i} - y_{j - 1} + 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126039} {:answer/id #uuid "d39c0e0d-56ed-5022-8689-6107c53f73d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x_{i - 1} - y_{j} + 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126040} {:answer/id #uuid "e66f9899-1378-5b70-a551-1e49c5f7b225" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of the options is correct" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126041} {:answer/id #uuid "141eb7b5-f3ce-59d9-b276-b8c46e582af5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x_{i} - y_{j} + 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126042} {:answer/id #uuid "637616b7-612d-53ce-88cc-a0e44190f529" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x_{i - 1} - y_{j - 1} + 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126043}] :answer-field/id #uuid "4d141b87-d83c-5dcf-b705-b4faa009947a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126038}] :question/id #uuid "d2fe7b45-b659-56e0-83bf-d42ccd4288ed" :question/math-academy-id "q-123746" :question/problem "Let $R = [0, 1] \\cdot [0, 1]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x, y) = x - y + 2$. Further, let\n\n$I = ∬_(R)f(x, y)dA$\n\nbe the unique number such that over all rectangular partitions $P$ of $R$, we have\n$L(f, P) \\le I \\le U(f, P)$,\nwhere $L(f, P)$ and $U(f, P)$ are the corresponding lower and upper Riemann sums, and\n\n$L(f, P) = ∑_(i = 1)^(m)∑_(j = 1)^(n)AAAAAΔx_{i}Δy_{j}$.\n\nWhat expression is missing from the double summation above?"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259568 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129175 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c0559f0c-a1ca-5ba8-a02e-71d584273958" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Double Integral Using Lower and Upper Riemann Sums"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "277b0f80-6ff9-5431-a0f7-34912bf8d55f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-40" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257128} {:answer/id #uuid "33e45ad5-f3b2-526a-ac85-a4c1b461b814" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257242} {:answer/id #uuid "5f1ad51b-7ae5-5511-bef4-dc805b3d1c70" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257616} {:answer/id #uuid "78b4d78b-7fe7-56ba-8344-a044f726bc81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257848} {:answer/id #uuid "ef327639-4a04-5689-9d0c-6e78432eca9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-48" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258858}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "78b4d78b-7fe7-56ba-8344-a044f726bc81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257848} :answer-field/id #uuid "802c169c-bbf7-558f-947a-0140a6d57f41" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259251}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "089ded76-3ed3-5ada-805a-37477a513dd6" :question/math-academy-id "q-123839" :question/problem "Let $R=[-1,3]\\times [2,5]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}},\\,{P}_{2}={{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the double integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ is a function such that ${m}_{ij}={M}_{ij}=-3$ for all partitions $P$ of $R,$ and ${m}_{ij}$ and ${M}_{ij}$ are the minimum and maximum values of $f$ respectively in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x,y),$ the double integral of $f$ over a rectangular region $R$ is the unique number $I$ (if it exists) such that\n\n$$\nL(f,P)\\le I\\le U(f,P),\n$$\n\nover all partitions $P$ of $R,$ where the lower and upper sums respectively are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{m}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} \\\\ U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{M}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand ${m}_{ij}$ and ${M}_{ij}$ are the minimum and maximum values of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nNow, since ${m}_{ij}={M}_{ij}=-3,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P)=U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(-3)\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} \\\\  & =-3({\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i})({\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}) \\\\  & =-3(3-(-1))(5-2) \\\\  & =-3\\cdot 4\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =-36.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\nL(f,P)=-36\\le {∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A\\le -36=U(f,P)\n$$\n\nwhich implies that\n\n$$\n{∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A=-36.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259569 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129175 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c0559f0c-a1ca-5ba8-a02e-71d584273958" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Double Integral Using Lower and Upper Riemann Sums"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4863d036-e3c0-54ea-9b68-c3d810c25830" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257417} {:answer/id #uuid "4985370e-205f-57cd-96e5-3dd1860f3c40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257425} {:answer/id #uuid "96b6bede-bb0d-536c-9929-13c0f977e7a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258113} {:answer/id #uuid "a8c42faf-b85f-56d6-b9cb-3abd2bfcc348" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258253} {:answer/id #uuid "c1771016-b30c-5b16-ad3d-44d9508f2a02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258475}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4985370e-205f-57cd-96e5-3dd1860f3c40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257425} :answer-field/id #uuid "ffcc488d-5039-58c5-9ed9-42126f86d743" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259483}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "bde095b1-d9b2-5272-b46e-003fde137023" :question/math-academy-id "q-123843" :question/problem "Let $R=[-5,-2]\\times [3,7]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}},\\,{P}_{2}={{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the double integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ is a function such that ${m}_{ij}={M}_{ij}=1$ for all partitions $P$ of $R,$ and ${m}_{ij}$ and ${M}_{ij}$ are the minimum and maximum values of $f$ respectively in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x,y),$ the double integral of $f$ over a rectangular region $R$ is the unique number $I$ (if it exists) such that\n\n$$\nL(f,P)\\le I\\le U(f,P),\n$$\n\nover all partitions $P$ of $R,$ where the lower and upper sums respectively are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{m}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} \\\\ U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{M}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand ${m}_{ij}$ and ${M}_{ij}$ are the minimum and maximum values of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nNow, since ${m}_{ij}={M}_{ij}=1,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P)=U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}1\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} \\\\  & =({\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i})({\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}) \\\\  & =(-2-(-5))(7-3) \\\\  & =3\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\nL(f,P)=12\\le {∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A\\le 12=U(f,P)\n$$\n\nwhich implies that\n\n$$\n{∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A=12.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259570 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129175 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c0559f0c-a1ca-5ba8-a02e-71d584273958" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Double Integral Using Lower and Upper Riemann Sums"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "071e0901-de13-55e8-b3d3-38e6553d7abd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "88" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256843} {:answer/id #uuid "4142d9d0-cec3-500e-a78b-ef11f652f069" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "72" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257362} {:answer/id #uuid "6749529d-0141-52b1-91d9-11f6330e3b4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257698} {:answer/id #uuid "6910c2c0-450e-5670-8806-08d7bb1b1918" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "96" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257715} {:answer/id #uuid "9641afa9-042b-520a-814f-00e707469578" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "108" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258102}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4142d9d0-cec3-500e-a78b-ef11f652f069" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "72" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257362} :answer-field/id #uuid "c7a338c3-5da7-5e36-ac5c-c953fdc59b0f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259378}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "198f001c-8f0a-5ac7-9854-7515cac5441b" :question/math-academy-id "q-123846" :question/problem "Let $R=[1,7]\\times [4,6]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}},\\,{P}_{2}={{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the double integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ is a function such that ${m}_{ij}={M}_{ij}=6$ for all partitions $P$ of $R,$ and ${m}_{ij}$ and ${M}_{ij}$ are the minimum and maximum values of $f$ respectively in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x,y),$ the double integral of $f$ over a rectangular region $R$ is the unique number $I$ (if it exists) such that\n\n$$\nL(f,P)\\le I\\le U(f,P),\n$$\n\nover all partitions $P$ of $R,$ where the lower and upper sums respectively are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{m}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} \\\\ U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{M}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand ${m}_{ij}$ and ${M}_{ij}$ are the minimum and maximum values of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nNow, since ${m}_{ij}={M}_{ij}=6,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P)=U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}6\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} \\\\  & =6({\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i})({\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}) \\\\  & =6(7-1)(6-4) \\\\  & =6\\cdot 6\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =72.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\nL(f,P)=72\\le {∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A\\le 72=U(f,P)\n$$\n\nwhich implies that\n\n$$\n{∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A=72.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186371679 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129220 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0b9d2e98-8007-51ec-bfb6-cb9b48029a2a" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Double Integral Using the Mean Value of X and Y"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dfe29d41-20aa-5404-b1fe-d53dd72a2e3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371681} {:answer/id #uuid "95247cc3-5d88-5219-8590-1f2e15220157" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371682} {:answer/id #uuid "d4dda20c-85d8-5cdb-8d70-c56d3857d27e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371683} {:answer/id #uuid "24f3cc9c-52d3-5832-98c6-6eaf7668b573" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371684} {:answer/id #uuid "5863543e-2974-5a76-a791-9bd5c9db01f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371685}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "95247cc3-5d88-5219-8590-1f2e15220157" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371682} :answer-field/id #uuid "7d7848e2-f768-55a9-aff3-ed72e02a83b6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371680}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "eeafd037-077a-51ed-84eb-4b9e62434000" :question/math-academy-id "q-123853" :question/problem "Let $R=[5,6]\\times [1,3]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)$ be a function defined over $R.$\nThe lower and upper Riemann sums corresponding to an arbitrary partition $P$ of $R$ are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(2{x}_{i-1}-3{y}_{j})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}, \\\\ U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(2{x}_{i}-3{y}_{j-1})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the definition of the double integral in terms of $L(f,P)$ and $U(f,P),$ compute ${∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.$\n\n*Hint: You may wish to make use of the following result:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}=({x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2})({y}_{n}-{y}_{0})\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x,y),$ the double integral of $f$ over a rectangular region $R$ is the unique number $I$ (if it exists) such that\n\n$$\nL(f,P)\\le I\\le U(f,P)\n$$\n\nover all partitions $P$ of $R.$\n\nFirst, notice that ${\\overset{¯}{x}}_{i}=\\frac{1}{2}({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})$ will always lie between ${x}_{i-1}$ and ${x}_{i}$, and similarly ${\\overset{¯}{y}}_{j}=\\frac{1}{2}({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j})$ will always lie between ${y}_{j-1}$ and ${y}_{j}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n2{x}_{i-1}-3{y}_{j}\\le 2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})-3\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j})\\le 2{x}_{i}-3{y}_{j-1}\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies to\n\n$$\n2{x}_{i-1}-3{y}_{j}\\le ({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})-\\frac{3}{2}({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j})\\le 2{x}_{i}-3{y}_{j-1}.\n$$\n\nMultiplying this by $Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}$ and applying the double summation gives:\n\n$$\nL(f,P)\\le {\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}[({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})-\\frac{3}{2}({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j})]Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\le U(f,P)\n$$\n\nSeparating the sums using the addition and constant multiple rules, we get\n\n$$\nL(f,P)\\le {\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}-\\frac{3}{2}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\le U(f,P).\n$$\n\nUsing the hint, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} & =({6}^{2}-{5}^{2})(3-1)=22 \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} & =\\frac{3}{2}({3}^{2}-{1}^{2})(6-5)=12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally then:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P)\\le 22-12\\le U(f,P)\\,⟹\\,L(f,P)\\le 10\\le U(f,P)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that \n\n$$\n{∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A=10.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129853 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129220 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0b9d2e98-8007-51ec-bfb6-cb9b48029a2a" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Double Integral Using the Mean Value of X and Y"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2bce989a-ccc8-55ff-a992-62b6d504521a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339509} {:answer/id #uuid "6aec35ab-8c69-595f-b18e-9434f98e2d47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "64" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340076} {:answer/id #uuid "8b6c1869-a2f7-5ec9-9775-3f07ec644566" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "48" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340378} {:answer/id #uuid "94c58dcc-23de-5bc1-8ca6-8ec5297eddcd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "80" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340465} {:answer/id #uuid "d9ab38c5-be1c-53eb-a2d7-362d22040bfb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "50" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341059}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "94c58dcc-23de-5bc1-8ca6-8ec5297eddcd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "80" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340465} :answer-field/id #uuid "c9c05c61-b32b-5fe2-821b-e8f8f940b2d2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341734}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "08870289-b60b-524f-b96e-8c75f1f41bc1" :question/math-academy-id "q-72627" :question/problem "Let $R=[0,4]\\times [0,2]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)$ be a function defined over $R.$\nThe lower and upper Riemann sums corresponding to an arbitrary partition $P$ of $R$ are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(4{x}_{i-1}+2{y}_{j-1})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}, \\\\ U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(4{x}_{i}+2{y}_{j})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the definition of the double integral in terms of $L(f,P)$ and $U(f,P),$ compute ${∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.$\n\n*Hint: You may wish to make use of the following result:*\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}=({x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2})({y}_{n}-{y}_{0})\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x,y),$ the double integral of $f$ over a rectangular region $R$ is the unique number $I$ (if it exists) such that\n\n$$\nL(f,P)\\le I\\le U(f,P)\n$$\n\nover all partitions $P$ of $R.$\n\nFirst, notice that ${\\overset{¯}{x}}_{i}=\\frac{1}{2}({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})$ will always lie between ${x}_{i-1}$ and ${x}_{i}$, and similarly ${\\overset{¯}{y}}_{j}=\\frac{1}{2}({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j})$ will always lie between ${y}_{j-1}$ and ${y}_{j}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n4\\cdot {x}_{i-1}+2\\cdot {y}_{j-1}\\le 4\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})+2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j})\\le 4\\cdot {x}_{i}+2\\cdot {y}_{j}\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies to \n\n$$\n4{x}_{i-1}+2{y}_{j-1}\\le 2({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})+({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j})\\le 4{x}_{i}+2{y}_{j}.\n$$\n\nMultiplying this by $Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}$ and applying the double summation gives:\n\n$$\nL(f,P)\\le {\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}[2({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})+({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j})]Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\le U(f,P)\n$$\n\nSeparating the sums using the addition and constant multiple rules, we get\n\n$$\nL(f,P)\\le 2{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}+{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\le U(f,P).\n$$\n\nUsing the hint, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} & =2({4}^{2}-{0}^{2})(2-0)=64 \\\\ {\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} & =({2}^{2}-{0}^{2})(4-0)=16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally then:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P)\\le 64+16\\le U(f,P)\\,⟹\\,L(f,P)\\le 80\\le U(f,P)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that \n\n$$\n{∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A=80.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186341844 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129175 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c0559f0c-a1ca-5ba8-a02e-71d584273958" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Double Integral Using Lower and Upper Riemann Sums"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e5b428c-4c23-5a83-be1c-6df4d762e86a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "128" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339688} {:answer/id #uuid "8c9fd21b-9417-56d3-84e1-840afddf0329" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "64" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340389} {:answer/id #uuid "8d814bf2-dc23-57a9-be7f-eba209974291" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340398} {:answer/id #uuid "d802acac-f768-50be-aef1-63a739271520" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341043} {:answer/id #uuid "f3331d03-1d50-5b8c-b595-1b8a7b69f007" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341271}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8c9fd21b-9417-56d3-84e1-840afddf0329" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "64" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340389} :answer-field/id #uuid "4a6a689f-7417-55ea-a529-00d56eb6642b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341510}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3273cb89-af5d-5582-86a1-9111196782fa" :question/math-academy-id "q-72684" :question/problem "Let $R=[0,4]\\times [2,6]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}},\\,{P}_{2}={{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the double integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ is a function such that ${m}_{ij}={M}_{ij}=4$ for all partition $P$ of $R,$ and ${m}_{ij}$ and ${M}_{ij}$ are the minimum and maximum values of $f$ respectively in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x,y),$ the double integral of $f$ over a rectangular region $R$ is the unique number $I$ (if it exists) such that\n\n$$\nL(f,P)\\le I\\le U(f,P),\n$$\n\nover all partitions $P$ of $R,$ where the lower and upper sums respectively are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{m}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} \\\\ U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{M}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand ${m}_{ij}$ and ${M}_{ij}$ are the minimum and maximum values of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nNow, since ${m}_{ij}={M}_{ij}=4,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P)=U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}4\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} \\\\  & =4({\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i})({\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}) \\\\  & =4(4-0)(6-2) \\\\  & =4\\cdot 4\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =64.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\nL(f,P)=64\\le {∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A\\le 64=U(f,P)\n$$\n\nwhich implies that\n\n$$\n{∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A=64.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186341884 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129220 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0b9d2e98-8007-51ec-bfb6-cb9b48029a2a" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Double Integral Using the Mean Value of X and Y"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1dfd4429-470e-5160-b38b-71b5f4ecfede" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-324" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339391} {:answer/id #uuid "51b20d0f-2079-5380-89c1-4228fc80f297" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-84" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339877} {:answer/id #uuid "a63a68b0-99d3-5209-8346-b98d891452b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-144" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340635} {:answer/id #uuid "b1d86d13-7214-5706-ae6b-1a73663bc8c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-360" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340747} {:answer/id #uuid "d88fee66-be60-57a1-ad55-13ef4e820d82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-168" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341051}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a63a68b0-99d3-5209-8346-b98d891452b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-144" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340635} :answer-field/id #uuid "e86449e4-c0a9-5b52-a8c2-80a206761f0f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341793}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "f6a79a2d-bcfd-5ef3-be20-8c72ffbf021f" :question/math-academy-id "q-72906" :question/problem "Let $R=[-5,-1]\\times [0,3]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)$ be a function defined over $R.$\nThe lower and upper Riemann sums corresponding to an arbitrary partition $P$ of $R$ are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(5{x}_{i-1}+2{y}_{j-1})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}, \\\\ U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(5{x}_{i}+2{y}_{j})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the definition of the double integral in terms of $L(f,P)$ and $U(f,P),$ compute ${∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.$\n\n*Hint: You may wish to make use of the following result:*\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}=({x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2})({y}_{n}-{y}_{0})\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x,y),$ the double integral of $f$ over a rectangular region $R$ is the unique number $I$ (if it exists) such that\n\n$$\nL(f,P)\\le I\\le U(f,P)\n$$\n\nover all partitions $P$ of $R.$\n\nFirst, notice that ${\\overset{¯}{x}}_{i}=\\frac{1}{2}({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})$ will always lie between ${x}_{i-1}$ and ${x}_{i}$, and similarly ${\\overset{¯}{y}}_{j}=\\frac{1}{2}({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j})$ will always lie between ${y}_{j-1}$ and ${y}_{j}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n5{x}_{i-1}+2{y}_{j-1}\\le 5\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})+2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j})\\le 5{x}_{i}+2{y}_{j}\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies to \n\n$$\n5{x}_{i-1}+2{y}_{j-1}\\le \\frac{5}{2}({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})+({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j})\\le 5{x}_{i}+2{y}_{j}.\n$$\n\nMultiplying this by $Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}$ and applying the double summation gives:\n\n$$\nL(f,P)\\le {\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}[\\frac{5}{2}({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})+({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j})]Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\le U(f,P)\n$$\n\nSeparating the sums using the addition and constant multiple rules, we get\n\n$$\nL(f,P)\\le \\frac{5}{2}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}+{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\le U(f,P).\n$$\n\nUsing the hint, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{2}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} & =\\frac{5}{2}((-1)^{2}-(-5)^{2})(3-0)=-180 \\\\ {\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} & =({3}^{2}-{0}^{2})(-1-(-5))=36\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally then:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P)\\le -180+36\\le U(f,P)\\,⟹\\,L(f,P)\\le -144\\le U(f,P)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that \n\n$$\n{∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A=-144.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129855 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129175 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c0559f0c-a1ca-5ba8-a02e-71d584273958" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Double Integral Using Lower and Upper Riemann Sums"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bc3ede01-6a29-5b22-bbdc-9b48974df0f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128612} {:answer/id #uuid "bc50c9e8-abe3-5b0f-9426-00dc38c5960c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128613} {:answer/id #uuid "e04c5f78-8b3a-5b3a-8f31-049ae226f210" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128614} {:answer/id #uuid "21fa0cd6-45de-5d9a-9996-3c6c45314878" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128615} {:answer/id #uuid "3cebd937-9cce-5a6f-ab14-e6e5a6c403e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128616}] :answer-field/id #uuid "2932f9cb-9b7f-515e-8253-dabbdcb75d5e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128611} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3353ca9f-51ab-51a8-9174-44f6fb3eee84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366262} {:answer/id #uuid "b35cb88b-3972-5e20-9788-60b4ea9b4c15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366263} {:answer/id #uuid "6d1b0a7a-b80d-5f8b-976e-7e14027e1304" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366264} {:answer/id #uuid "6e3cef94-383f-5d00-8fa0-399009bcce6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366265} {:answer/id #uuid "f3d468b6-4275-521c-b7f4-abeadf8f00f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366266}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f3d468b6-4275-521c-b7f4-abeadf8f00f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366266} :answer-field/id #uuid "e7b4be15-0b1e-5f67-9b68-ce3d1e514c8a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366261}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "74ebb72c-3651-5f76-b6c4-40ae9170b988" :question/math-academy-id "q-72910" :question/problem "Let $R=[-5,-2]\\times [-6,-1]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}},\\,{P}_{2}={{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the double integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ is a function such that ${m}_{ij}={M}_{ij}=3$ for all partitions $P$ of $R,$ and ${m}_{ij}$ and ${M}_{ij}$ are the minimum and maximum values of $f$ respectively in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x,y),$ the double integral of $f$ over a rectangular region $R$ is the unique number $I$ (if it exists) such that\n\n$$\nL(f,P)\\le I\\le U(f,P),\n$$\n\nover all partitions $P$ of $R,$ where the lower and upper sums respectively are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{m}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} \\\\ U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{M}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand ${m}_{ij}$ and ${M}_{ij}$ are the minimum and maximum values of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nNow, since ${m}_{ij}={M}_{ij}=3,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P)=U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}3\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} \\\\  & =3({\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i})({\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}) \\\\  & =3(-2-(-5))(-1-(-6)) \\\\  & =3\\cdot 3\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =45.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\nL(f,P)=45\\le {∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A\\le 45=U(f,P)\n$$\n\nwhich implies that\n\n$$\n{∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A=45.\n$$"}]}
